"SLUG-NAME-VERSION-FORMAT"                      =   "%@ - %@ (%@)";
"SLUG-ABOUT-MAIN-TEXT"                          =   "This is a simple countdown timer app. It counts down in seconds and sounds an alarm when it reaches zero. You can set timers up to 23 hours, 59 minutes, and 59 seconds.
    
Create as many timers as you like and organize them into groups, where they run sequentially. You can drag and drop timers between groups.

Each timer has two optional thresholds: a warning (yellow) and a final (red), indicating you’re nearing the end.

You can set short transition sounds between timers in a group, and a final ending alarm when all timers in a group finish.

There are three large, easy-to-read displays:
    • NUMERIC: A classic digital-style countdown.
    • CIRCULAR: A donut-shaped timer that disappears, as time passes.
    • STOPLIGHTS: Colored circles that change as thresholds are reached —ideal for debates.

To find out more, visit:
    https://riftvalleysoftware.com/rival-t



OPEN-SOURCE PACKAGES AND APP INFO:

The app relies on the following open-source Swift packages:

    •   https://github.com/RiftValleySoftware/RVS_BasicGCDTimer
    •   https://github.com/RiftValleySoftware/RVS_Checkbox
    •   https://github.com/RiftValleySoftware/RVS_Generic_Swift_Toolbox
    •   https://github.com/RiftValleySoftware/RVS_PersistentPrefs
    •   https://github.com/RiftValleySoftware/RVS_RetroLEDDisplay
    •   https://github.com/RiftValleySoftware/RVS_UIKit_Toolbox

Additionally, the app, itself, is \"source-available,\" and can be found here:

    https://github.com/RiftValleySoftware/ambiamara";

